# GPU/process core dumps - can contain raw GPU VRAM contents from
# whatever was loaded at crash time (potentially proprietary weight/
# kernel data), never committed. "gpucore.*" alone does NOT match
# "gpucore-<timestamp>.bin" (gitignore globs aren't regex - the "."
# is literal) - found live when a real captured devcoredump wasn't
# actually being ignored. Both naming schemes covered explicitly now.
gpucore.*
gpucore-*
core.*
*.core

# Proprietary binaries only ever belong here locally, never committed:
# danielblnc's own runtime builds, NVIDIA-derived weights, any extracted
# or patched build of either. See docs/linux-support-spec.md's
# "Scope of intent" section for the hard rule behind this.
windows-runtime-bridge/vendor/

# guentra/dlss5-amd-hip-linux's own real release binaries (MIT licensed,
# but still a separate, independently-versioned third-party project's
# compiled artifacts - fetched locally only for the backend-hookup
# verification experiment, docs/linux-support-spec.md §63, never
# committed here). ReShade's own real binary (reshade.me) is not MIT
# and definitely never belongs in this repo either.
windows-runtime-bridge/backends/guentra/vendor/

# The legacy OptiScaler-approach exploration and everything under it -
# real proprietary DLLs (danielblnc's own dlssnr_amd_pass*.dll) and a
# 147MB proprietary weights file live here locally. Never committed -
# this is exactly the mistake that leaked into the old repo's history.
windows/

# Wine/Proton build cache
*.cache

